From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:06:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/pf: Restore PF scheduling defaults when restoring auto
 provisioning

Any debugfs change to PF/VF scheduling (execution quantum, preemption
timeout, priority or the sched_if_idle policy) switches the PF into
custom provisioning mode. In custom mode, pf_disable_vfs() skips
xe_sriov_pf_reprovision_default(), so the PF keeps its custom scheduling
values after VFs are disabled.

Writing to the restore_auto_provisioning debugfs attribute switches the
mode back to auto and releases all VF configs, but it does not reset the
PF scheduling configuration. On the next VF enable, pf_needs_provision_sched()
finds non-default PF scheduling and skips fair scheduling provisioning:

  PF: Tile0: GT0: PF already provisioned with EQ
  PF: Tile0: GT0: PF already provisioned with PT
  PF: Tile0: GT0: PF and VFs 1-12 already provisioned with PRIORITY
  PF: Tile0: GT0: VFs 1-12 not provisioned with EQ
  PF: Tile0: GT0: VFs 1-12 not provisioned with PT

All VFs are then left with infinite execution quantum and preemption timeout.
During a VF FLR, the PF must clear the VF LMEM using its migrate queue,
but GuC never schedules that PF context, so the clear times out and FLR fails:

  PF: Tile0: GT0: VF24 resource sanitizing failed (-ETIMEDOUT)
  PF: Tile0: GT0: VF24 FLR didn't finish in 5000 ms (-ETIMEDOUT)
  PF: Tile0: GT0: VF24 control command FLR_START failed (-EIO)

The VF is left in an inconsistent state, the guest driver probe fails with
emit_wa_job -ETIME, and the following PF GT reset breaks subsequent VF enabling.

The same starvation also hits VF-to-VF: with sched_if_idle left enabled
and infinite VF EQ/PT, a VF probe fails even without any FLR:

  xe 0000:03:00.2: [drm] *ERROR* Tile0: GT0: hwe rcs0: emit_wa_job failed (-ETIME) guc_id=1
  xe 0000:03:00.2: [drm] *ERROR* SIGID=101 FATAL (-ETIME) PROBE: driver loading failed for device 'e20b'

Reproducer:

  echo 2 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:03:00.0/sriov_numvfs
  echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0000:03:00.0/gt0/pf/sched_if_idle
  echo 50 > /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0000:03:00.0/gt0/pf/exec_quantum_ms
  echo 0 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:03:00.0/sriov_numvfs
  echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0000:03:00.0/sriov/restore_auto_provisioning
  echo 2 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:03:00.0/sriov_numvfs

With a single VF the probe succeeds, but a subsequent VF FLR still fails
since the PF migrate job is never scheduled:

  echo 0000:03:00.1 > /sys/bus/pci/drivers/xe/unbind
  echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:03:00.1/reset

  PF: Tile0: GT0: VF1 resource sanitizing failed (-ETIMEDOUT)
  Tile0: GT0: Check job timeout: seqno=389, lrc_seqno=389, guc_id=0, not started

Reset the PF scheduling defaults (sched_if_idle, PF execution quantum
and preemption timeout) when switching back to auto provisioning, the
same way it is already done when VFs are disabled in auto mode. This
lets the next VF enable apply fair scheduling to PF and all VFs again.

Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_sriov_pf_provision.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_sriov_pf_provision.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_sriov_pf_provision.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_sriov_pf_provision.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_sriov_pf_provision.c
@@ -168,12 +168,19 @@ int xe_sriov_pf_provision_set_mode(struct xe_device *xe, enum xe_sriov_provisioning_mode mode)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (mode == XE_SRIOV_PROVISIONING_MODE_AUTO) {
+		int err;
+
 		if (xe_sriov_pf_num_vfs(xe)) {
 			xe_sriov_dbg(xe, "can't restore %s: VFs must be disabled!\n",
 				     mode_to_string(mode));
 			return -EBUSY;
 		}
 		pf_unprovision_all_vfs(xe);
+
+		/* custom PF EQ/PT/sched_if_idle would block fair VF scheduling */
+		err = pf_reprovision_default(xe);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
 	}
 
 	xe_sriov_dbg(xe, "mode %s changed to %s by %ps\n",
-- 
2.43.0

